@* Tasks asks its own module where entries live and the shared
   kernel what is turned on. It never sees the Inbox, Devbook or the Shell at
   all: what the Inbox routes here arrives through a port an adapter under
   src/Infrastructure answers, not through anything this project references.
   Now that the context is its own project these imports are the project's own
   rather than inherited from the desktop app, so what the pane needs is named
   here and nothing more. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using Microsoft.JSInterop
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Work.Abstractions.Tasks
@using global::Backlog.Modules.Work.Abstractions.Tasks.Services
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel
@using global::Backlog.Infrastructure.GitHub
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel.Markdown
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Markdown
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Selects
@* SelectionBar, the bulk-action bar above the list. Chrome only - the count,
   the live region, the way out of a selection and the indeterminate select-all
   that .devbook/design/interaction-guidelines.md#focus-and-selection asks for - and this
   pane fills its one slot with the selectors already imported above. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Selection
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Feedback
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Badges
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Buttons
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Inputs
@* Modal, for ImportPlanDialog — the pane's one dialog so far. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Overlays
@* SplitPane. Without this the pane rendered a literal <splitpane> element -
   Razor treats an unimported component as unknown HTML rather than failing, so
   the list and the detail pane stacked instead of sitting side by side. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Layout
@* TaskAction is the shape the storybook settled on for "add a step, put it in my
   day, remind me, give it a due date, repeat it" — one control for all of them,
   because a row that is set and a row that is not are two states of one thing. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Tasks
@* GoalControlSlot and GoalSubject: the hook a host cascades so the side panel can
   offer "Attach to goal" without this context seeing Goals. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Goals
@* IntegrationLink, for the pull requests and sessions an entry's work produced —
   drawn the way the Sessions pane draws them, so a PR looks the same wherever it
   shows up. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Integrations
@* ContextMenu and MenuItem, for the menu a right-click on an entry row opens. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Menus
@* The glyphs the scope chips wear in place of their words. *@
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Icons
@* DevbookReferenceChip, for the Devbook pages and chapters an entry points at.
   The library's component, not Devbook's screens: this project may not reach
   those, and a reference is drawn the same way wherever it is held. *@
@using global::Backlog.SharedKernel.Devbook
@using global::Backlog.UI.Components.Devbook
